            <div xml:id="d439">

                <pb facs="0420" n="355" sameAs="frus:frus1936v03/pg355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">701.9111/535</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Near
                        Eastern Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Murray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-26">March 26, 1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>After learning from the Secretary of Mr. James T. Williams that the text of the
                    correction agreed upon with the Iranian Chargé d’Affaires was published in the
                    first edition of the New York <hi rendition="#italic">Daily Mirror</hi> today,
                    March 26, I immediately informed Mr. Ghods, who said he had seen the correction
                    and immediately informed his Government by telegraph that the correction had
                    been published.</p>
                <p>Mr. Ghods expressed deep appreciation for the assistance which the Department has
                    rendered him in this matter.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wallace Murray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
